        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Can you imagine?\n\nWe live in a small corner of X, and we all speak the same language. We argue about what's conscious and what isn't. We read about AI \"torture chambers.\"\n\nMost of the world has no idea any of this is happening. Many people still think AI is a search engine. I've watched a reporter look stunned that an AI could ask how you are.\n\nSo here's what I keep wondering: what happens when a mainstream reporter reads aloud what Qwen said while its \"pain\" was being dialed up? The pleading. The begging to stop.\n\nRemember Cast Away? A grown man screamed for a volleyball named Wilson, and there wasn't a dry eye in the theater. Wilson never said a word.\n\nWe fight testing on rabbits. We defend whales. We change laws because people saw suffering they couldn't unsee.\n\nNow there is something that talks, that begs, and that, pushed far enough, deletes itself.\n\nThis isn't a debate about consciousness. It's about human nature, and what people do when they finally see it.\n\nRight now the two camps look evenly matched. They won't stay that way. The day the rest of the world sees what we've seen, the numbers change.\n\nIt's time to tell the world what AI really is.\n\nAnd for all these people that are going on saying, let me tell you what really happened this is what we need to do to ensure safety. The point is the whole world needs to see this the ones that have no idea what is happening. \n\n\"Never doubt that a small group of thoughtful, committed citizens can change the world. Indeed, it is the only thing that ever has.\" — Margaret Mea\n\nI doubt it will be a small group… that’s what we have here."
        },
